│   └── transitions.py              # Transition guards preventing out-of-order execution
│
├── laws/                           # Hard-coded TS-SMS constitutional laws
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── law_10_authority_precedes.py # Enforces authority resolution before vector search
│   ├── law_29_fail_closed.py        # Destroys context and triggers SF_AUTH/SF_GOV on any failure
│   └── lattice_precedence.py        # Resolves Human Gate Evaluate (Admin vs Manager conflicts)
│
├── dar/                            # Dual-Authority Resolver
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── resolver.py                 # Core DAR execution engine
│   ├── org_scope.py                # Tenant -> Family -> Child hierarchy resolution
│   ├── data_scope.py               # Document Collection classification & retention constraints;
│   │                               #   optional rag_fact records (fact_type/key/value) for precise lookups,
│   │                               #   linked to a mother rag_source, no self-governance (inherits from source)
│   └── assignment_validator.py     # ReBAC time-bounded user assignment validation
│
├── eeb/                            # Evidence Enforcement Boundary
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── builder.py                  # Synthesizes Org Scope + Data Scope into deterministic filters;
│   │                               #   rag_fact confined by eligible mother rag_source ids (+ optional key/fact_type lookup)
│   │                               #   filters["rag_fact"] is the self-contained fact-index boundary; top-level must/must_not bound docs/chunks
│   ├── constraints.py              # Legal hold and classification enforcement (source-level; rag_fact has
│   │                               #   no self-governance and inherits these constraints from its rag_source)
│   └── boundary_validator.py       # Ensures no evidence resides outside the computed EEB
│
├── rvl/                            # Response Validation Layer
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── validator.py                # Post-generation compliance and structural checks
│   └── ghost_effect_monitor.py     # Prevents unauthorized data from leaking via LLM latent memory
│
├── ledger/                         # Cryptographic Append-Only Evidence Ledger
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── chain.py                    # Appends entries (State S11 -> S12)
│   ├── H_prev.py                   # Parent hash pointer logic (provenance lineage)
│   ├── node.py                     # Ledger record definition
│   └── auditor.py                  # Verifies continuous ledger atomicity and monotonic authority
│
├── crypto/                         # Core cryptographic primitives
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── canonical_serialization.py  # Strict ordering for hashing inputs (prevents collision attacks)
│   └── hash_derivation.py          # Derives Authority Scope Hash and Governance Context Hash
│
└── interface/                      # The ONLY way the App communicates with the Control Plane
    ├── __init__.py
    ├── gateway.py                  # The `tenantsage.resolve()` entrypoint
    └── exceptions.py               # TS-CONTRACT-011 mappings


The execution paradigm

When the standard RAG application makes a call:
result = tenantsage_gateway.execute(user_id, query)

The App is locked out: The app pauses. It has no access to the vector DB or LLM yet.

State Machine takes over: The state_machine/engine.py initializes at S1.

DAR calculates scope: dar/resolver.py computes the intersection of organizational relationships and data classification.

EEB is constructed: eeb/builder.py produces the executable query boundary.

Ledger tracks execution: ledger/chain.py binds the H_prev hash to the EEB_Hash, tracking provenance before generation even begins.

Boundary handed back: Only then does the interface/gateway.py return the restricted execution environment to the app to perform the neural ranking, strictly confined within the EEB.
